"""AI-sandbox only (the user never runs this). Compiles native-android/PlaybackService.java against tiny hand-made stubs of Android / Media3 (no Android SDK here;
there is no `javac` binary, but the JDK module works) and RUNS the earphone-button logic with a fake player + fake clock:
  boAt BassHeads 225 (wired, one button: 1 / 2 / 3 presses), TRIGGR Kraken X1 + Ultrabuds N5 (Bluetooth: PLAY / PAUSE / NEXT / PREVIOUS per gesture), key-up events, empty queue.
The stubs follow the real API from memory: trust it for "does it compile" and "does the press logic do what the manual says", NOT for real phone behaviour.
Run from the project root: python3 tests/java-probe-earphones.py"""
